{
  "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
  "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:50 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Title IX is violated by retaliatory action against Coach Jackson."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But -- but that's again the question of the substantive scope of the provision, and that's different from whether there was a congressional intent to create a private cause of action for this sort of violation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Irving L. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Retaliation against a person because that person has complained about sex discrimination under title IX is itself discrimination within the meaning of title IX."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "never been imposed under title IX."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why would Congress then in some statutes expressly cover retaliation and in others not? I mean, that's a little odd, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What was the date of the Sullivan case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What implication would there be, if we took the view of the circuit here, for Federal employment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what -- what do you make of the -- the point that Mr. Dellinger stressed and others have stressed that, in fact, there is no administrative remedy in the real world?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0001-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And -- and again, it's on a motion to dismiss, and obviously, once it was --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is this a civil rights statute that provides for a private cause of action?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Of course, you say it's not there, but the agencies interpreting the statute thought it was there. Isn't that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. THOMAS (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. THOMAS: Well, Justice Breyer, on the face of the statute, I just can't get there. I apologize for that, respectfully, but -- but I can't."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the case was affirmed by the Eleventh Circuit and this Court denied cert in 1997"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kevin C. Newsom (Amicus Curiae for Alabama)",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is to clarify some things about the scope of the administrative remedy. The other side, with respect, wants you to think that without the implied right of action for damages and fees, whistle blowers are left out in the cold. That is not true. The administrative remedy -- it's not just about funding termination. 34 C.F.R. 106.3 says that the OCR may use any remedy that it deems necessary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dellinger",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The last point they make is that even if there's a cause of action, and even if the cause of action covers retaliation, it cannot be brought by Coach Jackson because he's not also the victim of the underlying discrimination. That makes no sense in law or in logic."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dellinger",
      "case_id": "2004-02-1672",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b7ab7bd8c04d52d93c2dc2647e062f81570d743f470f281eae4f8cf031366410",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b7ab7bd8c04d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they've both been discriminated against on the basis of sex because they're trying to rectify sex discrimination or neither is."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
